                    Senior Xero Accountant / Hands-On Bookkeeper – Australian SME | Part-Time

About us

Build Technics is an established Melbourne commercial maintenance and building-repair business. We work with commercial property managers, facilities managers and repeat business clients.

We are looking for one experienced Philippines-based accountant or senior bookkeeper to personally take ownership of our Xero records and provide accurate, practical financial information to our Directors.

This is a small, long-term part-time role—not a full-time position and not an agency engagement.

The role

This is not an FP&A, virtual CFO or strategy-only role.

You must genuinely enjoy working hands-on in Xero: reconciling accounts, reviewing coding, locating discrepancies, cleaning up records and ensuring the underlying accounts are reliable.

Once the books are clean, you will also prepare concise management reports and identify issues that require action. You will not be expected to make local debt-collection calls. A Melbourne-based Business Support & Operations Lead will use your reports to follow up clients, suppliers and internal staff.

Our Australian BAS agent will continue to manage payroll, superannuation, BAS lodgement and specialist GST matters. Your responsibility is to maintain clean, reconciled accounts and provide an organised BAS-period handover.

Expected hours

• Initial clean-up and handover: up to 12 hours per week for the first four to six weeks.

• Ongoing: expected to average 8–10 hours per week, with some variation around month-end and BAS periods.

The actual ongoing requirement will be reviewed after the first six weeks once transaction volume, clean-up requirements and automation opportunities are understood. Hours above the agreed weekly cap require prior approval.

• Work will generally be completed across two or three agreed blocks each week.

• Monday and Tuesday availability is useful so financial exceptions can be available before our Wednesday team meeting.

• Some overlap with Melbourne business hours will be required during onboarding.

• Once the role is established, we expect mainly asynchronous communication and a short monthly review—not unnecessary weekly meetings.

• Hours above the agreed weekly limit require prior approval.

This may suit someone who works for an Australian accounting firm and wants one stable private client. However, you must disclose your current employment and other ongoing clients, confirm that outside work is permitted, and reliably complete our work personally.

Responsibilities

Hands-on Xero ownership

• Take over routine Xero processing from our existing administration support.

• Review and clean up the current Xero file.

• Reconcile bank accounts, credit cards, payment-clearing accounts and relevant balance-sheet accounts.

• Review transaction coding and correct or query inconsistencies.

• Maintain reliable accounts payable and accounts receivable records.

• Ensure bills, invoices and receipts are attached or correctly linked to the relevant transaction.

• Maintain a clear missing-document and unresolved-transaction list so our local team can obtain the information.

• Review Xero rules and recommend sensible improvements without overcomplicating the system.

• Ensure reconciliations are current and unexplained balances do not accumulate.

Practical accounting treatment

• Correctly distinguish cash received from revenue earned.

• Correctly recognise customer commencement deposits and supplier prepayments.

• Reconcile deposits against final invoices and supplier bills.

• Understand the treatment of client deposits, supplier deposits, GST and final invoicing.

• Identify material unfinished jobs requiring a simple WIP or accrued-revenue adjustment.

• Our usual billing structure is straightforward: an initial commencement deposit and a final invoice—not numerous progress claims.

• Be capable of supporting more structured job accounting if we later move from ServiceM8 to Simpro.

Month-end and management reporting

Prepare a concise monthly financial pack showing:

• reconciled profit and loss;

• balance-sheet exceptions;

• cash position;

• aged receivables and aged payables;

• customer and supplier deposits or prepayments;

• material WIP or incomplete-job issues;

• unusual margin, coding or timing issues;

• missing documents and decisions required;

• practical working-capital or cash-exposure concerns.

We do not want long reports produced for their own sake. We want reliable numbers, clear exceptions and short explanations in plain English.

BAS and external bookkeeper support

• Prepare clean, reconciled accounts for our Australian BAS agent.

• Provide an organised list of outstanding queries before each BAS period.

• Understand Australian GST and BAS requirements well enough to identify likely issues.

• Work constructively with our BAS agent when a transaction requires specialist treatment.

• Support the annual TPAR process once the core accounts are stable.

Process improvement

• Learn our current Xero, OFX and payment-processing workflow.

• Document the current process before recommending changes.

• Help simplify the flow between supplier invoices, payment approvals, OFX and Xero.

• Improve financial controls without creating unnecessary administration.

• Work with ServiceM8 initially and potentially Simpro in the future.

• Maintain concise process notes in Microsoft 365/SharePoint.

Role boundaries

You will not be responsible for:

• making debt-collection or supplier follow-up calls;

• managing our Australian office staff;

• approving or releasing payments;

• providing technical building or job-pricing decisions;

• replacing our BAS/payroll agent;

• producing complex FP&A models or corporate-style board reports;

• delegating our work to another person.

No agencies, bookkeeping teams or subcontracting arrangements will be considered. The successful person must personally perform and review the work.

Required experience

You must have:

• at least three years of substantial Xero bookkeeping or accounting experience;

• direct experience working with Australian businesses;

• preferably experience inside an Australian accounting or bookkeeping firm;

• strong bank, card, clearing-account and balance-sheet reconciliation skills;

• sound understanding of Australian GST and BAS requirements;

• experience preparing month-end accounts and useful management reports;

• the ability to identify issues rather than simply process transactions;

• strong written English and the ability to explain accounting issues clearly;

• an accounting degree or equivalent relevant experience;

• reliable internet, equipment and secure working practices;

• the confidence to work independently without hiding unresolved items.

Xero certification is highly regarded.

Experience with ServiceM8, Simpro, construction, trades, maintenance or another job-based business would be useful but is not essential.

The person we want

We are looking for someone who is:

• careful but not painfully slow;

• confident enough to question something that does not make sense;

• practical rather than overly theoretical;

• able to distinguish an important exception from ordinary bookkeeping;

• honest about errors, workload and unresolved questions;

• comfortable working directly with business owners;

• interested in building a stable, long-term relationship with one Australian business.

Remuneration

AUD $10.00-$17.00/hr per hour, depending on demonstrated Australian accounting and Xero experience.

The initial practical assessment will be paid at the agreed hourly rate. Ongoing hours will be agreed and capped in advance.

Selection process

Shortlisted candidates will complete a small paid practical exercise using dummy information. It will include:

• a customer commencement deposit;

• a supplier deposit;

• an unfinished job at month end;

• a final client invoice;

• several reconciliation and missing-document issues.

You will be asked to explain:

• how you would record and reconcile the transactions in Xero;

• the likely GST/BAS considerations;

• how they should appear in management reporting;

• the difference between the accounting profit and the immediate cash position;

• what questions or documents you would request from us.

How to apply

Begin your application with the words BT XERO so we know you have read the full advertisement.

Please answer each of the following:

1. How many years have you worked with Australian businesses in Xero?

2. Have you worked directly inside an Australian accounting or bookkeeping firm? Explain your role and the work you personally completed.

3. Describe the balance-sheet accounts you normally reconcile at month end.

4. Briefly explain how you would treat a customer commencement deposit and a 50% supplier deposit for an unfinished job.

5. What is your current employment, and how many other private clients do you currently service?

6. Confirm that you will personally perform all Build Technics work and will not subcontract or delegate it.

7. State your weekly availability, preferred working blocks and expected hourly rate.

8. Provide your resume and details of any Xero certification.

Generic applications that do not answer these questions will not be considered.
